I believe I have come up with an incantation which gets past the problem
of RedHat Install hanging while formatting one's root partition. (I had
been having this problem intermittently with my Seagate ST32250N
installed in my AS 200/166.)

(If disk is already partitioned correctly, skip to step 3.)

Step 1: Begin installation procedure.

Step 2: Partition disk with fdisk. Write partition information back to
disk.

Step 3: Power computer off and back on.

Step 4: Begin installation procedure.

Step 5: Enter fdisk, then exit with "q" option.

Step 6: (This is the key.) Spin around in your chair 3 times, each time
reciting: "Please work. Pretty please with sugar on it."

Step 7: Finish installation procedure.

Randy C.



