There is a big difference in how things get laid out when partitioning
with fdisk and with disklabel.  I'm not savvy on the details, but
suffice it to say that the partition tables have different encodings
and different locations on disk (IIRC, fdisk-style partition
information is located at the start of the disk, while the disklabel
is stored at the end).

I'd guess that one could put a disklabel on a fdisk-ed hard disk
drive, but I've never done it before and I don't have any spare disk
drives I want to go mucking about on.

