headswitch: 0           # milliseconds
track-to-track seek: 0  # milliseconds
drivedata: 0 

6 partitions:
#        size   offset    fstype   Size(Kb)   Size(Mb)
  1:     4494        0  resrvd13       2247       2.1   # (Cyl.    0 - 1)
  2:   262899     4494      swap     131449     128.3   # (Cyl.    2 - 118)
  3:  8388315        0    unused    4194157    4095.8   # (Cyl.    0 - 3733*)
  4:   103362   267393      ext2      51681      50.4   # (Cyl.  119 - 164)
  5:  2096451   370755      ext2    1048225    1023.6   # (Cyl.  165 - 1097)
  6:  5921109  2467206      ext2    2960554    2891.1   # (Cyl. 1098 - 3733*)
---end minlabel---

Note that sdb4 is root, sdb5 /usr, and sdb6 /var.  Here's the command
I use to update the boot area:

	swriteboot -f1 -f3 /dev/sdb /boot/bootlx /vmlinux.gz

With a total size of 1,011,417 bytes, so ~2MB should be plenty of
room.  Using an uncompressed kernel instead gives a total of
2411KBytes, which isn't enough room the way I've got things
configured.  But there's no reason to not use a compressed kernel.
Aboot knows how to decompress gzipped kernel images.

