I've discovered the problem on my system. I used dmesg to display the
IRQ being used by my PCMCIA cards. I have a SCSI card and a combo
Modem/Ethernet card. All 3 devices share the same interrupt. If I remove
the SCSI AND reboot, the problem goes away. If I have the SCSI inserted
but I do not use the SCSI bus, the system works fine. As soon as I use
the SCSI card, the system must be rebooted to get the ethernet card to
work.

It seems that you may have a similar problem, not knowing how an
Alpha is setup, I can't say for sure.

Good luck.

