When we simulate our physical models we do some property decomposition
and have to submit a large number of independent simulation jobs,
e.g. investigation of temperature behavior of a model substance
requires  about 12 independent runs of the same system at different
parameters. That means, there are *2* independent jobs on a dual box,
we had never more than 3% loss (!) compared to single job. But, if
you need to split *1* job into processor threads - this is a 
completely different story.


> Then the ratings become $100 / SpecFP (dual PII/400 without case) 
> and $82 / SpecFP (Alpha 533LX with 2meg cache and case)

This does not hold, after my knowledge ;-)

