Ok.  It's just that there seem to have been a number of "How do I
address memory directly, like under DOS?"-type requests lately.  If
you check the manpage for mmap, it appears to indicate that you pass
it a base address, a length and some flags & it returns the address
you should use in your local space (ie, the one it mapped to).  Other
posts seem to indicate that such programs need to be setuid root.  Not
actually having used this stuff myself, I'm not the final authority
(but that's no reason no to conjecture. ;) ).

