2.0.33, redhat 5.0, and sysklogd 1.3-25 (and 19) when we would remote log
from a busy machine.

After changing syslogd.conf to log everything locally the problem went away.

I had traced it down to a problem where select would get a single bad fd
(application that was writing to syslog closed, or network socked closed)
and syslogd would try to read/write to/from the fd.

