   I'm running RedHat Alpha 4.2 on a PC124.  Concerning compiling            
   a new kernel, the file /usr/src/linux/README is an intel file  
   rather than an alpha file, and the directions given are false.
   In particular 'make' has no rule for 'zImage'.  So what does
   one substitute for 'make zImage'?                                                   

Way back when I actually had an alpha...


You need to make sure that the top level Makefile has

ARCH=alpha

as the architecture to compile for.

Second, you just do a :

make vmlinux

Then (and my memory is getting real hazy here), you then
need to run:


make bootimage


to get a kernel suitable for booting from.

