Getting close to having my new UDB 166 fully up to speed and ready to
replace my old 486 and SPARC boxes.  Got X working on my crappy SVGA
monitor but wanted to use my 20" SUN monitor with it and in theory the
TGA card on the UDB should work.

Turns out it does!

Hunting about on the net I found a page of interest:

http://www.iaehv.nl/users/leibbran/sunmon/sunmon.htm

These provided the necessary information to do the job.

My monitor has the annoying SUN combination connector on the back rather
than nice easy BNCs but I got an old SUN cable, hacked the end off and
fitted a VGA plug according to the instructions on the webpage.  Having
played around on a multisync with the UDB I had a good idea of where to
start and got the thing going with the second Modeline I tried, my
monitor doesn't go out to 1280x1024.

Here are the two Modelines that work very well:

# 1024x768 @ 76 Hz, 62.5 kHz hsync
Modeline "1024x768"   85  1024 1056 1176 1352  768 772 775 811

# 1152x900 @ 76 Hz
Modeline "1152x900"   94  1152 1212 1312 1536  900 912 928 964 -hsync

Of course, I use the latter but its good to have choices :-)

The only downside is that console mode doesn't work yet but I should be
able to get that going with SVGAtext.  Currently I just leave the thing
in X via xdm.

All in all, very pleased, works like a charm and will do until I can
afford to put a 24bit card in to replace the TGA.

This UDB is great fun :-D

-- 
Dr. Shane Sturrock - sss@holyrood.ed.ac.uk
