> Hi,
> I have a Alpha Box with 1GB RAM running RedHat 5.0. Even when I am not running
> any jobs (besides the window manager plus a few xterms) "free" reports almost
> all of the memory in use:
>              total       used       free     shared    buffers     cached
> Mem:       1032968    1016336      16632      49200     729128      76752
> -/+ buffers/cache:     210456     822512
> Swap:       263160          0     263160

Linux, like most modern OSes, uses memory to buffer disk blocks.
That's using almost all of your memory, but should a program want to
use that memory, it would still be available. You want to look at the
"free + buffers" number, which is 822.5 megabytes available.

-- g



