http://www.specbench.org/osg/cpu95/results/cfp95.html

They have the 533MHz SX board listed at 16.1, I would expect the 
LX to be ~10-15% faster.  Based on this result, however, you
could buy 533MHz SX Alphas with $$/SpecFP = $56 (this includes the 
case an power supply - $895).  See www.dcginc.com for details.
That is, if you're basing all your purchasing decisions on spec numbers,
which I wouldn't do.  You'll get the best results be running your
code across multiple platforms.

Jeff



