In a previous article, "Rob Richards" <rrichards@cwaretech.com> said:
>I have a UDB box with Redhat 5.0 installed.  X seems to be configured
>properly, yet when I start it, it will eventually fail with the message that
>the MemBase for the TGA card needs to be set (or something to that effect).
>It also says to check the /proc/pci file.

Do what it says.  Look at /proc/pci and make a note of the memory base.  Mine
looks like:

PCI devices found:
  Bus  0, device  11, function  0:
    Display controller: DEC TGA (rev 2).
      Medium devsel.  Fast back-to-back capable.  Master Capable.  Latency=15.  
      Prefetchable 32 bit memory at 0xa000000.
[snip]

See that "32 bit memory at 0xa000000"?  It may be a different value on your
machine.  Take note of it.  Now go to your config file (which is linked all
over the place, but /usr/X11R6/lib/X11/XF86Config is one place to find it),
and set that value as the MemBase.  The appropriate part of mine looks like:

Section "Device"
    Identifier  "TGA"
    VendorName  "DEC"
    BoardName   "ZLXp-E1"
    MemBase     0xa000000 
    #VideoRam    2048
    # Insert Clocks lines here if appropriate
EndSection

-- 
