In article <35577A68.44E@rocketmail.com>, PoPy  <popym@rocketmail.com> wrote:
>I can't install linux
>Milo begin to load and it stop
>The screen print PALCODE ....

How are you starting the load process? On an SX164 (PC164SX),
I was successful running linload.exe directly off of the CD; set
up a boot selection, specify the path to the loader on the CD at

\milo\arc\linload.exe

Specify the "OS load file" as (device path doesn't matter; you can set
it to be the CD; I believe linload always gets it from the same device
or partition):

\milo\lx164

Then boot from that selection. That should get you in to MILO; you can
set the "boot options" to be

boot -t iso 9660 XXX:/kernels/lx164.gz root=/dev/XXX

(where XXX is whatever is your CD) or you can enter that in once you're in
MILO (which you may need to if you're not sure of the Linux device name).

That will start the installer.



