In a previous article, S S Sturrock <sss@holyrood.ed.ac.uk> said:
>I just inherited a UDB 166MHz with 16MB of RAM and 500MB SCSI disc.  It
>has RedHat 5.0 installed and boots OK but doesn't have X configured.

The UDB video board is a TGA.  There is a TGA driver for it with RedHat.  Run
XConfigurator, and tell it "Unlisted Server", and then later on it will ask
you which server and you pick TGA.  I'll attach my XF86Config file on the end
of this post.  You have to find the memory address ofyour PCI slot by looking
in /proc/pci, and then changing the MemBase parameter in your X config file
accordingly.

The TGA card only supports 8 bit planes, but does so at very high resolution.
I'm running 1280x1024, but I believe it will do 1600x1200 as well.

As for PCMCIA cards, I've read conflicting reports - the RedHat documentation
seems to be saying no, but there appears to be PCMCIA support in the kernel
now.


