>>>>> "Homonnai" == Homonnai Mihaly <homer@unicorn.sch.bme.hu> writes:

Homonnai> Does anybody run TGA in 1600x1200? What is the relevant
Homonnai> config for this resolution?

I've not tried any of these lines on a TGA, but they work well on my
Millenium-II (on a K6 box):

#====================================================================
# 1600x1200 @ 67 Hz, 82.36 kHz hsync
Modeline "1600x1200"  170    1600 1616 1744 2064  1200 1202 1206 1230

# 1600x1200 @ 72 Hz, 88.26 kHz hsync
Modeline "1600x1200"  185    1600 1664 1792 2096  1200 1204 1209 1234

# 1600x1200 @ 76 Hz, 93.99 kHz hsync
Modeline "1600x1200"  200    1600 1680 1808 2128  1200 1204 1210 1240

# 1600x1200 @ 81 Hz, 99.43 kHz hsync
Modeline "1600x1200"  210    1600 1664 1808 2112  1200 1204 1211 1242
#====================================================================

Note that after adding that block to the XF86Config file, you must
edit the relevant Screen section and change the Modes line to use
the value "1600x1200".

I translated the modelines above from a config file for AccelX; even
so they come without warranty of any kind.

If the TGA is not capable of a 170+ MHz clock rate, I also have the
data for a 60 Hz version of the above, but have not translated it.  (I
only went as low as my monitor required.)

-JimC
