"James Sternberg" <jsternbe@atomic1.phys.utk.edu> wrote:

> Does anyone here know of a good set of compilers for alpha-linux?  We have
> recently purchased a DEC XL 300 and installed Linux on it, but the code
> which gcc and g77 produce is very slow.  As a matter of fact, using gcc and
> g77 on my PC at home (only a Pentium 233MMX) and compiling the code for my
> research produces an executable which is about 20% faster on the Intel box
> than the Alpha.  This does not make much sense.

Which gcc/g77 combo do you use ?  You won't get any performance out of 
g77-0.5.2[012] + gcc-2.7.2.3 on Alpha's because of a design problem in the 
handling of the combination of 64-bit pointers and 32-bit array indices (not 
that it would generate wrong code, it's just painfully slow).

Try egcs-1.0.2 for a better solution (or, if you can wait a week, egcs-1.0.3) 
- http://egcs.cygnus.com

