Check out this link http://www.digital.com/semiconductor/alpha/  . 

I think the  211PC you are referring to is the 21164PC chip and runs on
the alpha 164 SX motherboard. The alpha 21164 processor runs in the 164
LX board. The primary differences between the to is the LX has at least
a 2 meg L3 cache while the SX has a 1 meg L2 cache and no L3. There is 
about a $600 to $1000 difference in price between the two depending
where you look. The LX is faster, costs more, and has a little more
hardware compatibility then the SX. Both of them will run linux well but
if you plan to make a server out of this box I'd recommend the LX board
for the extra performance. I personally run a 21164 LX system with 128
megs RAM, SCSI UW bus, and a 8 meg fire gl card. I built it myself for
around $2,500. You can purchase one like mine similarly equipped from
$2800 to $3100 w/o monitor. check out www.alphapowered.com for links to
alpha resellers. 

