>>>>> "CMR" == Charles M Richmond <cmr@iisc.com> writes:

    CMR> So when using GNUS to connect to an NNTP server that requires
    CMR> a USER and PASSWORD authentification, how does one get gnus
    CMR> to either prompt for or preconfigure the needed answers.

That's pretty easy.  Add 'nntp-send-authinfo to
'nntp-server-opened-hook and make certain 'user-login-name is bound to
the proper string.

Since not all my servers use authentication, and since I have
different usernames for different things, I use the following select
method rather than set the variables correctly (e.g. with addhook and
setq)

(setq gnus-select-method '(nntp "news.newsguy.com"
				(nntp-server-opened-hook (nntp-send-authinfo))
				(user-login-name "xenophon")))

For more information, see (gnus)NNTP for the gory details.

(You should have no problem figuring out which Gnus and EMACS version
I'm using.)

