	Well, I'm running RH 4.2 on this an had absolutely no troubles
beyond when I first partitioned the disks.. I was a newbie to scsi and had
to figure out the drive parameters to enter in to fdisk since it didn't
auto recognize them from the drive.  
	I'm running Linux 2.1.88 on it right now and it's been very
stable.. mostly just acts as a file server for my home lan. I've got
three 4 gig drives joined together in a raid-0 device, and haven't had any
troubles at all with that.  (I've got a 1 gig drive that came with it as
the boot drive though and a spare 4 gig in it for scratch space. (don't
ask.. onsale had a sale on drives and I went beserk)) 
	BTW: all the 4 gig drives are obviously in an external case.. I
was worried about overheating when I had two hard drives in there because
they got VERY hot.. not a lot of cooling in there so it's probably best to
move a second drive to an external case if possible.  1 is fine though. 
   
