I can't answer the question WRT FORTRAN per se. However, the alpha
chips  do not support the IEEE infinities, NaNs, and denormals directly.
They generate a trap. In Digital Unix and Linux, the kernel contains
contains the IEEE exception handler for IEEE. First, the compiler must
be told to generate FP instructions with the /S modifier. In DUX, the
options are -ieee, -ieee-with-no-inexact and -ieee-with-inexact
On GCC, the option is -mieee.  The most current Alpha chip (EV6) does
understand infinities.
-- 
