>

 If this has already been answered forgive me; I didn't see the reply.
I ran into the same problem when I installed both of these systems.  It is
actually very simple - if you choose the simpler installation - where you
select general classes of software instead of the select individual
packages
option - you don't get the "mtools" package installed by default.

What you can do is do an install and after you choose the classes of
software
you proceed to choose the option to select individual packages.  You will
be
prompted to select from all of the package classes.  Look for "mtools" this

package contains the msdos tools especially mkfs.msdos.  Forgive me for
I don't know exactly which category of packages you will find mtools
under.

Better yet, if you can find the name of the RPM in whichever distribution
you
are using just use rpm -Ivh <mtools_rpm_name>.

