According to Michael Champigny <champigny@cadsys.enet.dec.com>:
>I'm not sure why Mozilla is not yet stable on Alpha...maybe Lesstif-0.84
>will help things a bit when it's released.

A big hint is looking at how Mozilla is compiled on Digital Unix: with
"-taso", which basically tells the compiler and linker to make all
addresses fit in 31 bits, so that things that break on 64 bit platforms
will work.  There is no equivalent option for gcc.  I think that a lot
of the problems are that a) Mozilla itself is not all that stable yet,
and b) Mozilla is not 64 bit clean.
