3) Go into the OS setup menu
4) press insert to insert a new os
5) put a label of something like linux-a (to signify you're booting from
the
    a: drive)
6) change the boot drive to a:
7) change the bootloader to \linload.exe
8) change the os drive to well..anything really...it shouldn't matter
    put the os path to \, shouldn't make any difference either.
    leave the boot parameters blank

9) It will complain about something or other when you save it.
10) put the milo/linload boot disk in the a: drive.
11) Select the linux-a OS from the os boot menu...the a: should
      kick into action
12) when it gets to the milo prompt type
       boot fd0:vmlinux.gz root=/dev/fd0 load_ramdisk=1 prompt_ramdisk=1
13) Insert ramdisk when it asks for it.
14) install linux.
15) After reboot, assuming  the root partition was installed on the first
    partition of the first ide disk (hda1......sda1 if scsi) do
    boot hda1:vmlinux.gz root=/dev/hda1

16) after its booted, mkdir /mnt/dos ; mkdir /mnt/floppy if
  not already there.
  i)  mount the dos patition you created right at the very start
  on /mnt/dos (mount /dev/<device> /mnt/dos>
  ii) insert the milo/lilo floppy in the a: if you've taken it out.
  iii)mount /dev/fd0 /mnt/floppy
  iv)cp /mnt/floppy/linload.exe /mnt/dos/
     cp /mnt/floppy/lilo.exe /mnt/dos/

17) reboot
18) Back in alphabios, create a new boot os in the os configuration
    bit.
    label linux
    boot loader device to the dos partion
    boot loader path to \linload.exe
    ospath to anything
    set the boot parameters
    boot hda1:vmlinux.gz root=/dev/hda1

19) save it...and reboot....and that should be it...all installed


NB: You'll need to use the new pc164 (I think) milo from dec.com
    for it to work, else screwie thing will happen.

Hope my memory was good enough to get you further than you
managed to get before.


